// meownary detection catalog.
//
// This file is data, not code. Each entry names a byte or text pattern, where
// to look for it, what it means, and why we believe it. The scan builds one
// matcher over every pattern and reports at most one finding per entry per
// file, at the first offset where the pattern appears. Findings carry the
// signature id "catalog.<id>".
//
// Field rules, checked by the validator and a test:
// - id: unique, lowercase, dotted, such as "packer.upx".
// - kind: the category the finding falls into (BrandPacker, Bundleware, ...).
// - confidence: strong, moderate or weak. A strong entry must list at least
//   one "sig:<id>" item in corroboration, naming another entry that has to
//   match in the same file. When any named entry is missing, the finding is
//   reported as moderate and the note says why. Free text in corroboration is
//   documentation only. A lone string is moderate at most; heuristics are weak.
// - severity: info for brand facts, notice for removable junk, warn for
//   bundleware and tamper strings.
// - formats: the format labels the entry applies to. An empty list means any
//   file, including files with no recognised format.
// - detect: Text(needle, window) for a UTF-8 string, or Bytes(hex, window)
//   for raw bytes in lowercase hex. Patterns are at least 4 bytes and match
//   case-sensitively. The window is Header (first 64 KiB), Tail (last 64 KiB)
//   or Whole (both). Nothing outside those windows is read.
// - source: a real URL that documents the pattern or the tool behind it.
// - false_positives: what benign content can also match, when that is known.
// - removal: None unless blanking the matched bytes is clearly safe. RawBlank
//   overwrites the match in place with fill (default 0x00; 0x20 inside text),
//   and Truncate cuts the file at the match. Both need a non-empty formats
//   list, and a match at offset 0 never gets a marker.
(
    signatures: [
        // Packers and protectors.
        (
            id: "packer.upx",
            kind: BrandPacker,
            confidence: strong,
            severity: info,
            formats: ["pe", "elf", "macho"],
            title: "UPX-packed executable",
            detect: Text(needle: "UPX!", window: Whole),
            corroboration: ["sig:packer.upx0", "sig:packer.upx1", "UPX names its PE sections UPX0 and UPX1"],
            source: "https://github.com/upx/upx/blob/devel/src/conf.h",
            false_positives: Some("The bytes \"UPX!\" can occur in unrelated data. ELF and Mach-O builds have no UPX0/UPX1 section names, so they stay moderate."),
            removal: None,
        ),
        (
            id: "packer.upx0",
            kind: BrandPacker,
            confidence: weak,
            severity: info,
            formats: ["pe"],
            title: "UPX0 section name",
            detect: Text(needle: "UPX0", window: Header),
            source: "https://github.com/upx/upx/blob/devel/src/pefile.cpp",
            false_positives: Some("A section can be renamed to anything; on its own this only hints at UPX."),
            removal: None,
        ),
        (
            id: "packer.upx1",
